# LUX visual system

Client sites should read as intentional and premium, not templated. When
building or restyling UI, default to these unless the client's own brand
overrides them.

## Type

- Display / headings: **Archivo** (tight tracking, heavier weights for impact).
- Body / UI: **Inter**.
- Mono / technical accents: **IBM Plex Mono**.
- Establish one clear type scale. Don't mix more than these three families.

## Aesthetic

- Industrial / machined: generous whitespace, a strong grid, confident
  hierarchy, restrained color.
- Sharp, deliberate spacing over decorative flourish. Let structure carry the
  design.

## Color

- Pull the client's brand palette into theme tokens first. If none exists,
  default to a high-contrast neutral base: near-black ink, clean white, one
  accent.
- Maintain AA contrast minimum on all text.

## Per-client override

A client's own brand guidelines always win over LUX defaults. When client tokens
exist in `tailwind.config`, use them and treat this rule as the fallback only.
